  "findings": "Independent AI Lean review by /root/backlog_review; I did not author FORM-1 through FORM-3, the H2 Lean additions, capture harness, source map or terminal receipt. I independently recomputed the exact current native/current union: all 208 entries match live source and review-source-map.json SHA-256 61a3fab748a022dae692fa3422b34c8824803c0a0570f66431d26fc7e048c6a7. I examined both actual changed formal owners, decision_risk.lean and variational_duality.lean, their catalogue exports and maturity records, and the current H2 terminal/projection signatures. This is a detailed audit of the new proof additions and their boundary contracts, with a focused review of the unchanged H2 baseline exports; it is not a fresh line-by-line audit of every baseline proof. The relative-support density bridge handles shared zero atoms explicitly, derives native absolute continuity and the Radon-Nikodym identity, and preserves native infinity in the separate singular-support theorem. The embedded product, joint and channel bridges supply unrestricted finite mutual-information garbling; finite KL processing still requires relative input support. Arbitrary deterministic and sparse channel rows are admitted through normalization rather than positivity certificates. The deterministic identity and unit-coarsening witnesses state the totalized finite KL convention and do not erase its distinction from extended native KL. The new optimization proof establishes zero-safe entropy continuity, closed coordinate feasibility, bounds every feasible mass by one, and obtains an attained minimum from compactness plus a feasible witness. The dual lower bound comes from an actual bounded-below Lagrangian infimum; its nonnegative distortion/multiplier and nonempty-code zero-multiplier assumptions are explicit. The Boolean quarter-budget theorem derives existence and positive information, without declaring the explicit crossover witness optimal; half-budget nonuniqueness and zero-budget uniqueness follow from concrete laws and constraints. No new axiom, opaque assertion, unsafe declaration or proof placeholder appears in these two owners. I independently ran three existing native consumer tests with the pinned toolchain and shared deadline runner: sparse relative-support/native-information consumer, rate-distortion optimization consumer, and full-support finite-channel consumer; 3 passed in 41.19 seconds with their warning-free assertions. The current scalar H2 terminal keeps distinct parameter-learning and latent-state posteriors; its Fin4 export uses the precise fixed precision/covariance carrier and conditional-law equality almost everywhere. The scalar projection specializes the all-ones embedded input line; it does not derive arbitrary full-state projection. Stationary grid initialization and coordinate reversal do not prove nonstationary path evolution or physical reverse dynamics. I separately verified every capture artifact digest, the equal 173-entry native before/after maps, identical collection/run bytes, and the strict validate_test_evidence result of 329 complete mandatory cases. Actual JUnit has 329 cases with zero failures/errors/skips and duration 412.045 seconds. I explicitly approve the H2-only collection migration and its clear separation from the whole-suite publication gate: the harness freezes the complete MANDATORY_TEST_FILES collection before execution, enables the heavy Fin4 consumer, clears inherited selections and disables plugin autoload/live providers; an accepted capture does not itself grant terminal acceptance. Approval is only for this exact H2 source union and its Lean evidence/boundaries. Numerical diagnostics remain explanatory non-proof evidence; terminal sealing, continuous G0 eligibility, H3 protocol freeze, provider operation, full-suite coverage, hosted CI and publication require their own checks. No source bytes outside this reviewed union or future changes are approved.",
